)+10(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=5{x}^{2}-4x+5\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n10\\alpha {x}^{2}+(12\\alpha +10\\beta )x+(2\\alpha +6\\beta +10\\gamma )=5{x}^{2}-4x+5\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10\\alpha =5\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,{x}^{2}) \\\\ 12\\alpha +10\\beta =-4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ 2\\alpha +6\\beta +10\\gamma =5\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =\\frac{1}{2},\\beta =-1,\\gamma =1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-x+1.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by \n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3x}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-x+1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371251 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371251 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371251 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371251 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371251 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371251 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371251 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371251 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186371255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371251 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a7d23e8b-11b4-5ec1-a02e-b04b713d3e20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371252 #edb/ref 1080 "y={e}^{-3x}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371252 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371252 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "98457a6f-2eb2-5f65-b07b