 be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha ,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=0\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$  and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n0+2\\alpha +(\\alpha x+\\beta )=3x+4\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives:\n\n$$\n\\alpha x+(2\\alpha +\\beta )=3x+4\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\alpha =3\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ 2\\alpha +\\beta =4\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =3,\\,\\beta =-2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=3x-2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404580 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404580 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404580 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404580 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404580 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404580 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404580 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404580 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404580 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b3a0d7ea-2403-5870-baf3-f1e3941ec6cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404581 #edb/ref 1080 "{y}_{p}=3x-10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404581 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404581 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "934ee56b-b088-5533-ad4c-e3032ce0c524" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404582 #edb/ref 1080 "{y}_{p}=-2x+3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404582 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 175921